 ### [MASt3R Feature Integration](15806-mast3r-feature-integration.md)
-Enriches stereo matching cost volumes with deep multi-view features from the MASt3R foundation model. It addresses limitations of traditional cost volumes by injecting semantically rich correspondences, particularly effective for weak texture or repetitive patterns.
+MASt3R Feature Integration is a method for enriching stereo matching cost volumes with deep multi-view features to improve depth estimation and subsequent mesh reconstruction accuracy. It addresses the limitation of traditional cost volumes by injecting semantically rich correspondences learned by the MASt3R foundation model, which establishes dense pointmap and stereo feature correspondences between image pairs. Unlike monocular feature integration (e.g., DINOv2), which extracts features from single images, this method leverages pairwise multi-view consistency, making it particularly effective for scenes with weak texture or repetitive patterns where local photometric costs are ambiguous.
 
